  <section id="tooling">
  
  <h2>30. Tooling &amp; ecosystem</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Concern</th><th>C#</th><th>TypeScript</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>SDK / compiler</td><td><code>dotnet</code> CLI (SDK, runtime, build, test, publish)</td><td><code>tsc</code> (check+emit), <code>tsx/bun</code> for running</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Packages</td><td>NuGet (<code>dotnet add package X</code>)</td><td>npm / pnpm / yarn / bun + jsr</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Test</td><td>xUnit, NUnit (<code>dotnet test</code>)</td><td>Vitest, Jest, Node runner, Playwright</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Lint / format</td><td>Roslyn analyzers, <code>dotnet format</code></td><td>ESLint, Biome, Prettier, <code>tsc --noEmit</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Web</td><td>ASP.NET Core (controllers, minimal APIs, Blazor)</td><td>Express, Fastify, Hono, Next/Nuxt/Astro (this site!)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>ORM / data</td><td>EF Core, Dapper</td><td>Prisma, Drizzle, Kysely, TypeORM</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Config</td><td><code>appsettings.json</code>, env, user-secrets</td><td><code>.env</code>, <code>process.env</code>, dotenv + zod schemas</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <h3>JSON: typed vs validated</h3>
  <Compare>
    <div slot="left">
      <pre><code>using System.Text.Json;
var user = JsonSerializer.Deserialize&lt;User&gt;(json)!;
string back = JsonSerializer.Serialize(user);

// source-generated (AOT-friendly):
[JsonSerializable(typeof(User))]
partial class UserJsonContext : JsonSerializerContext &#123; &#125;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div slot="right">
      <pre><code>// JSON.parse returns any — always validate!
import &#123; z &#125; from "zod";
const User = z.object(&#123; id: z.string(), name: z.string() &#125;);
type User = z.infer&lt;typeof User&gt;;
const user = User.parse(JSON.parse(json)); // throws if bad
const back = JSON.stringify(user);</code></pre>
    </div>
  </Compare>
  <h3>HTTP APIs</h3>
  <Compare>
    <div slot="left">
      <pre><code>// Minimal API (ASP.NET Core)
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
var app = builder.Build();
app.MapGet("/users/&#123;id&#125;", (string id) =&gt; Results.Ok(new &#123; id &#125;));
app.Run();</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div slot="right">
      <pre><code>// Hono (or Express/Fastify — same shape)
import &#123; Hono &#125; from "hono";
const app = new Hono();
app.get("/users/:id", (c) =&gt; c.json(&#123; id: c.req.param("id") &#125;));
export default app;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </Compare>
  <h3>File I/O + DI + testing</h3>
  <Compare>
    <div slot="left">
      <pre><code>// sync + async files
string t = File.ReadAllText("a.txt");
string t2 = await File.ReadAllTextAsync("a.txt", ct);

// DI built-in
builder.Services.AddScoped&lt;IRepo, Repo&gt;();

// xUnit
[Fact] public async Task Creates() &#123; Assert.Equal(1, 1); &#125;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div slot="right">
      <pre><code>import &#123; readFile &#125; from "node:fs/promises";
const t = await readFile("a.txt", "utf8");
// sync version exists but blocks event loop — avoid

// DI: manual or tiny libs (no built-in container)
// Vitest (xUnit-like):
// import &#123; test, expect &#125; from "vitest";
test("creates", () =&gt; &#123; expect(1).toBe(1); &#125;);</code></pre>
    </div>
  </Compare>
  <ul>
    <li>C# serialization is typed end-to-end. TS <code>JSON.parse</code> is <code>any</code> — validate at the boundary.</li>
    <li>C# DI is built into ASP.NET; TS relies on constructor injection by hand or minimal helpers.</li>
  </ul>

